# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository, and checked out as LF
# everywhere — including Windows, where core.autocrlf=true would otherwise
# rewrite them to CRLF on the way to the working copy.
#
# This is not a style preference. app/security.py pins SHA-256 hashes of the
# worker's protected files, and the worker refuses to start when they do not
# match. With autocrlf rewriting bytes between the repository and the disk, the
# same commit produces different hashes on different machines, and a clean
# clone can fail to start with nobody having changed a line. The hash function
# now normalises line endings too, so this file is the belt to that suspenders:
# either alone fixes it, and having both means neither has to be perfect.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Genuinely binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.mkv binary
*.webm binary
*.avi binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
